{
  "koral-function": 1,
  "purpose": "Instancing",
  "description": "What of an Instances function's instances is seen this frame, worked out on the GPU: clusters out of sight or past drawDistance left out; one wholly past pointDistance that spans fewer pixels than it has instances, as many points as it spans; and of the rest each instance its mesh when nearer than pointDistance, a point when further. So there are never many more points than pixels, however many instances. Gives the meshes' indirect draw (commands, one) and which instance each drawn one is (visible), and the points for SplatPoints. toClip is the Instancer's entity's matrix, then the view, then the lens; indexCount, firstIndex and vertexOffset are the mesh's (a MeshBuffers'); capacity and pointCapacity how many of each there is room for.",
  "tags": [
    "instancer",
    "instances",
    "cull",
    "frustum",
    "lod",
    "level of detail",
    "points",
    "gpu driven",
    "indirect"
  ],
